A||||8||theogre||Tranny oil/fluid
Z||000000||theogre||08-01-99||02:57 PM||||If you haven't changed the tranny oil yet. Do It.<p>In the manual tranny, the oil simply gets old. New oil can help shifting, and is just a good idea after so many years.<p>In the TH125 Auto tranny, it can make a major diferance in the performance of the car. Why? Well, new oil is always good in a auto tranny, but in this case, you get better oil. The new oil, Dexron 3, is all around better than the Dexron 2 that's likely in the tranny now. In a good tranny, it's very likely you'll get better shifting, and better performance from the Torq Converter.<p>Recently I changed the oil in my 87 TH125, and was very suprised at the diferance it made. Using the pump to drain the tranny, I was able to extract over 5.5 quarts of fluid. That's most of the total volume of the tranny. Even tho you leave some old oil behind, you at least now have almost 6 quarts of new oil.
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-02-99||07:52 AM||||You're not kidding, Ogre!  When I bought my V6 SE 4-sp it would crunch going into second gear and was very difficult to get into first.  The gear oil was thick and black.  I drained it and replaced it with 5W-30 Valvoline and it shifts nice and slick now - no more "Cap'n Crunch."  You wouldn't think gear oil would make that big a difference in a manual gearbox.
Z||000002||Bruce||08-02-99||11:08 AM||||What is the oil capacity of the 4 speed?
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-03-99||08:04 AM||||I feel like an idiot saying this, but I just filled it up until the oil level hit the "full" mark on the speedo sending unit that doubles as a dipstick.<p>I'm sure my Haynes manual lists a capacity.  I'll have to remember to bring that to work tomorrow so I can tell you what it is.
Z||000004||ChadMan||08-05-99||07:13 AM||||I'm a day late.  But Haynes lists a capacity of 3 qts for the 4-sp and recommends filling it with 5w30 motor oil.
Z||000005||Bruce||08-05-99||09:56 AM||||Thanks, Chad!
Z||000006||BlackGT||08-05-99||10:48 AM||||Hello People,<br>I may sound like an idiot but I have no idea<br>where to put the manual fluid or where this<br>dipstick is...some one enlighten a newbie!<br>Thanks!!
Z||000007||theogre||08-05-99||03:10 PM||||the manual units w/o a dip stick fill thru the speedo sender hole. there are 2 marks on the sender that indicate low & full.
Z||000008||theogre||08-05-99||03:17 PM||||BTW..... the correct method for installing the neck seal for the new auto tranny filter is to push the seal into the tranny, and then push the oiled neck of the filter into the seal. If you try it any other way you'll likely wreck the new filter.
